om":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T19:43:27-07:00","id":1412205,"title":"","content":"I am very excited and glad this is out but $40 for a pdf is very steep in the asking price especially given how it looks like rules are still a bit hazy and rushed in certain places.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3239-jane_dargason","name":"Jane_Dargason","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3239_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-10T00:25:19-07:00","id":1412811,"title":"","content":"So i looked through the pdf, it's beautiful but some of the roles are a bit hazy, the inanimae were removed from being playable in the beta, there was no mention of the baku or lorelei, selkies aren't just a camp of pooka, nothing on customizing kiths or kith blessings anymore, there was a mention of actual Fomorians as antagonists which was pretty nifty, the Thallain are a bit.... God awful in my humble opinion, the arts seem neat but a bit weird in places, not really digging no chimerical death or reincarnation since that was a huge part of changeling and the whole reason for the changeling way even existing in the fist place.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of where they were going with winter having come and the worlds of flesh and dreams becoming much more hostile to the fae but I do feel that this is an incomplete product in many places and needs an errata or an expansion or something to tweak and iron out some of the kinks in it.<br /> <br /> Beautiful book, wouldn't say it's worth $39.99 but it's really nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3239-jane_dargason","name":"Jane_Dargason","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3239_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-10T17:04:02-07:00","id":1412930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jane_Dargason</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1411150-met-changeling-larp-corebook-now-live?p=1412811#post1412811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So i looked through the pdf, it's beautiful but some of the roles are a bit hazy, the inanimae were removed from being playable in the beta, there was no mention of the baku or lorelei, selkies aren't just a camp of pooka, nothing on customizing kiths or kith blessings anymore, there was a mention of actual Fomorians as antagonists which was pretty nifty, the Thallain are a bit.... God awful in my humble opinion, the arts seem neat but a bit weird in places, not really digging no chimerical death or reincarnation since that was a huge part of changeling and the whole reason for the changeling way even existing in the fist place.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of where they were going with winter having come and the worlds of flesh and dreams becoming much more hostile to the fae but I do feel that this is an incomplete product in many places and needs an errata or an expansion or something to tweak and iron out some of the kinks in it.<br /> <br /> Beautiful book, wouldn't say it's worth $39.99 but it's really nice.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> could you give a list brief summary of the arts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T08:12:37-07:00","id":1414740,"title":"","content":"Curious did they advance the metaplot? I know Mage MET did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T11:12:04-07:00","id":1414764,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it's set during the endless Winter. It doesn't entirely follow on from the Time of Judgment events since it says that Winter began at the turn of the millennium (which originally was the arrival of the Adhene, etc.). But basically Y2K hits, banality ravages the world, and has some fundamental mechanical effects on changelings like locking them into their primary legacy so they can't change courts easily anymore, and also it stops changelings from reincarnating, so dead is dead now. High King David mounts some expedition to the Deep Dreaming on some quest because of some vision of a solution or something, but dies (or is killed). Then Meilge reveals himself as head of the Shadow Court and reveals the Shadow Court has been stockpiling glamour for decades in anticipation of Winter. The Shadow Court philosophically welcome Winter as a necessary step to a new spring. They offer to share their resources and protect the kithain in exchange for fealty, which the populous accepts. I think that's most of the metaplot updates but I've mostly skimmed it so far. There are lots of references to the Fomorians awakening, possibly tying that to reincarnation stopping. <br /> <br /> It also takes the opportunity to do like, it's own overhaul of the game system much as C20 did, with some headline changes. Seems like there are five seemings now (foundling, errant, wilder, eidolon, legend), which is basically a background that's also sort of like...reputation? It's a combined &quot;you've been in changeling society for X amount of time and are Y level of respect&quot; and it affects downtime actions and skill costs in addition to how much glamour and banality you have. Temporary banality is now called ennui. Permanent banality is just called banality. <br /> <br /> Also, I happened to read the piskies write-up and WOW ARE THEY DIFFERENT. Piskies are now the <i>human souls displaced by Sidhe</i>. Well, any changeling that got to where they are by kicking out a human soul wholesale rather than by merging with them, but obviously that's mostly the sidhe. Which uh, given them an interesting perspective on fae and humans, and especially on the individual sidhe who stole their body. Which...is an interesting idea, honestly. <br /> <br /> I'm not sure it's particularly where I, personally, would most want the metaplot to go? But it's definitely an interesting direction based on what I skim read.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-20T13:28:13-07:00","id":1414791,"title":"","content":"Hmmm Very interesting!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T00:58:51-07:00","id":1415275,"title":"","content":"So they didn't really change anything much from the pre-release versions despite all the feedback and its still mind numbingly wrist slashing depressing.....and the Piskie thing is just deeply weird. On the whole it reads like somebodies edge-lordy home-brew campaign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-28T17:15:12-07:00","id":1415904,"title":"","content":"Ok. So I see from their character sheet they added a new Realm called condition? How is it work. Also as I understand it every Kith has a &quot;Kith Art&quot; thus adding a whole bunch of new ones? What was added? I am kind of interested in taking bits of it.. but would like to know more how well these might adapt back","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-29T02:26:53-07:00","id":1415955,"title":"","content":"As I said I don't think it's where I'd go with it personally but I have some respect for the idea of just pushing on past Time of Judgement in canon rather than sort of ignoring it as C20 did. Again, to be clear, I prefer C20's setting, but I don't think the idea is inherently home-brewy and I kinda think some of the ideas are interesting. The nothing of everything being frozen because it's Winter meaning Changeling's aren't coming back, that they can't easily shift legacies, is interesting. As is the idea that everyone's beholden to the bad guys. Because it means the bad guys have power but 1) can't kill all the good guys because no one's reincarnating and 2) can't convert all the good guys because everyone's legacies are frozen. That's...interesting to me.<br /> <br /> And honestly I really like the idea of the piskies being human souls that have been so changed by their experiences they're basically fae now. Even C20 changed the piskies a lot because the original versions were really generic. So yeah, screw it, do something bloody weird?<br /> <br /> As to the Arts and Realms, the mechanics of it are set up to work with LARPing so it's pretty different. Basically cantrips are just spells. Realms are optional add-ons that empower or let you use a cantrip in a number of interesting ways, but they're not as necessary to the system as they are in the tabletop version. Actor lets you use a cantrip in unexpected circumstances - kind of like a sneak attack. Fae powers up your cantrips. Nature lets you use it against targets you wouldn't normally be allowed to. Prop lets you make magic items. Condition lets you cast a cantrip to go off when a condition is fulfilled. Scene is the same - multiple targets. Time makes cantrips last longer. <br /> <br /> When you make a character you get the first dots of three Kith-aligned arts automatically and can buy up to level 5 with starting or earned experience. You can buy up to level 3 in non-Kith-aligned arts with experience. You need a teacher to learn those, I think. And I think there's also a system of &quot;commoner&quot; vs &quot;noble&quot; arts with you needing a teacher to learn arts from the other category. <br /> <br /> And yeah, like...the arts are just ALL redone, pretty much. I mean a lot of the core and additional arts still exist (Chicancery, Primarl, Soothsay, Sovreign, etc.) but some a lot of the cantrips have been rewritten, although the flavour is the same. And then there's loads of new ones. I can't recall them all but there's Inglenook which is like a Hearth-and-Home Art. Dread which I think is for Sluagh. Oakenshield seems to be its own Art now (though Primal is still around). So that's all pretty different and yes, could probably be backported to tabletop though you'd have to rewrite the mechanics since it's all been rewritten to work for LARP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-29T07:35:17-07:00","id":1415971,"title":"","content":"From what i have heard i think the clurichain change is actually good? The Current one is... abit.... racist? While the BNS version makes them obsessed with contracts. Which makes them.. more interesting.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the Piskey thing... if you start pointing out their connection to the SIdhe... it kind of hard to ignore the Boggan connection too... all three are based on stuff we call elves, one might even include clurichain in them make them function like Mehune as a single kith with a Noble variant or Like the Eshu... actually with the contract obssesed Clurichain you have the estates.. Those who Rule(Sidhe) those who work(boggan) those who 'Pray&quot;(Clurrichain) and Outlaws(Piskeys)<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm kind of interested in what new powers they developed and maybe taking inspiration for builds. Like if they came up with a better Infusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-17T07:42:28-07:00","id":1418660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jane_Dargason</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1411150-met-changeling-larp-corebook-now-live?p=1412811#post1412811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So i looked through the pdf, it's beautiful but some of the roles are a bit hazy, the inanimae were removed from being playable in the beta, there was no mention of the baku or lorelei, selkies aren't just a camp of pooka, nothing on customizing kiths or kith blessings anymore, there was a mention of actual Fomorians as antagonists which was pretty nifty, the Thallain are a bit.... God awful in my humble opinion, the arts seem neat but a bit weird in places, not really digging no chimerical death or reincarnation since that was a huge part of changeling and the whole reason for the changeling way even existing in the fist place.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of where they were going with winter having come and the worlds of flesh and dreams becoming much more hostile to the fae but I do feel that this is an incomplete product in many places and needs an errata or an expansion or something to tweak and iron out some of the kinks in it.<br /> <br /> Beautiful book, wouldn't say it's worth $39.99 but it's really nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh where can you see the Changling MET beta?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T04:29:03-07:00","id":1418804,"title":"","content":"The Alpha and Beta slice content was originally up on the Storyteller's Vault site for free, but has been removed, I think, now that the final book has been released.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}